      "edition": "The Well and the Shallows (London: Sheed & Ward, 1935), as transcribed by Project Gutenberg Australia (Roy Glashan, 2013).",
      "description": "Introductory note and 40 essays (the 'My Six Conversions' series grouped as one part); site furniture and contents dropped. The text in sources/en-US-originals/ is the plain-text extraction of the page's paragraphs and headings (HTML tags removed). Titles set in title case from the transcription's capitals.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Public domain by author's death: Chesterton died in 1936, so the text has been public domain in Brazil, the UK, the EU, Canada and Australia for more than 70 years. In the US the 1935 book is still within its 95-year term (to 1 Jan 2031) unless unrenewed; no renewal was found in the Copyright Office records (see research/sourcing/chesterton.md). Imported under README decision 3."
    }
